Package: rehydra
Type: Package
Title: Resistance, Recovery and Resilience Indices for Drought-Rewatering
        Cycles in Plants
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person(
    given = "Joao Everthon da Silva",
    family = "Ribeiro",
    email = "everthonribeiro10@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Quantifies drought damage, resistance, recovery, resilience and
    physiological memory in plant time series subjected to one or more
    drought-rewatering cycles. Resistance, recovery and resilience indices are
    computed following Lloret, Keeling and Sala (2011)
    <doi:10.1111/j.1600-0706.2011.19372.x>, drought-rewatering concepts follow
    Xu, Zhou and Shimizu (2010) <doi:10.4161/psb.5.6.11398>, and the
    drought-memory stability framework follows Ingrisch and Bahn (2018)
    <doi:10.1016/j.tree.2018.01.013> and Ribeiro and others (2021)
    <doi:10.1016/j.jplph.2021.153397>. The package
    adds recovery-period and total-reduction components, mean-reduction and
    mean-recovery-rate components, damage- and recovery-curve shape descriptors
    (deficit area under the curve, time to half recovery, exponential recovery
    rate constant and response latency), automatic or manual segmentation of
    successive cycles, between-cycle memory indices, bootstrap confidence
    intervals, designed-experiment analysis of the indices including mixed
    models for repeated cycles, multivariable composite scores, diurnal
    detrending of sub-daily series, replication planning, publication-ready
    graphics, automated reports and a 'shiny' interface.
